# Multiversal Passage: "As this land enters, choose a basic land type. Then you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it
# enters tapped. This land is the chosen type."
#
# The first paragraph is one replacement effect (CR 614.1c, 614.12): the type is chosen, then the 2 life is paid or
# not, in the order printed, and nothing asks which applies first. Naming Island makes the land an Island (CR 305.7),
# and nothing on the card says "{T}: Add {U}" — that ability comes from the subtype (CR 305.6), which is what tapping
# it for blue at the end proves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Multiversal Passage
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Multiversal Passage.Play
Bot1.Modes(Island)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Battlefield.Multiversal Passage.Activate

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot1.Mana = {U}
Bot1.LandsPlayed = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Multiversal Passage
Bot1.Battlefield.Multiversal Passage.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Multiversal Passage.Types = Land
